ce or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 07 Proofread by  SELIM NASSER  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue  designated as axillary sampling  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior orange  inferior green  The specimen is sectioned two separate hard spiculated irregular nodules in the central region of the breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm repectively  These nodules are more than 0 7cm from the closets margin which is the depp margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is firm  representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Inferior margin B  Superior margin C  Medial margin D  Lateral margin E  Smaller nodule with deep margin F  Deep margino G  Anterior margin H N  representative sections from firm breast tissue  O  2 nodes P  2 nodes Q  1 node II  3 nodes CC FF HH  Larger nodule DD EE  Fibroadenoma Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional latera left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal no focal lesions  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes R BB  Resident  LYNN CORNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL TISSUE   EXCISION , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 46 CLINICAL DATA  Previous lumpectomy  DCIS at margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  NODULAR ADENOSIS HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY BREAST  RIGHT  EXCESS TISSUE    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  LACTATIONAL CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SKIN WITH SCAR AND SUTURE GRANULOMAS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 98 at 12 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a mastectomy specimen measuring 20 x 20 x 8cm with an ellipse of skin measuring 10 x 7cm and unremarkable nipple area  Along the medial surface of the specimen there is an area measuring 8 x 8cm that looks like a cystic wall and is focally calcified  Sectioning reveals diffuse  white to hemorrhagic  soft areas occupying about 40  of the total specimen  and present on the posterior inked margin  along the broad front  8 x 6cm    White  soft material is being released from this area upon applying pressure  SECTION CODE A C  Comedo like tumor on the posterior inked margin  E G  Firm  white  focally hemorrhagic area  H  Firm  white area with closest posterior margin  I  Unremarkable breast tissue  J  Skin with adjacent unremarkable breast  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast skin excess tissue  are multiple fragments of skin measuring in aggregate 12 x 6 x 1cm  One of the fragments contains scar measuring 9 x  2cm  Representative sections are submitted in K through M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast excess tissue  are multiple fragments of breast tissue with skin ellipses measuring in aggregate 16 x 12 x 5cm and weighing 400 grams  Representative sections are submitted in N through W  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCESS TISSUE   PART C  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION , Present.
