also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate mass  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm grossly abutting against the anterior resection margin  Representative sections taken at the anterior margin is frozen as FX  1  and resubmitted in cassette A  Additional representative sections with both the anterior and posterior margin is submitted in cassette B  Additional sections of the tumor in C and D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm sacular shaped  fibroadipose tissue with orienting stitches  two short stitches   lateral  one short and one long stitch   superior  two long stitches   deep margin  two small stitches inside previous biopsy cavity    There is no grossly apparent tumor   Dr  Carter reviewed the specimen in the Frozen Section Lab  and agrees with the gross diagnosis   The entire specimen is inked black  The medial half of the previous biopsy cavity surface is double inked blue  the lateral half surface of previous biopsy cavity is double inked green  The superior  deep  margin is double inked red  Section code  E  anterior margin extending to medial margin F  anterior margin extending to lateral margin  with a 0 2cm cystic cavity at the deep margin  G  anterior margin extending to superior margin H  anterior margin  extending to inferior margin I