Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 55 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast invasive ductal cancer  Status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  1 6cm by measurement on slides  Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Not indicated  BREAST  LEFT MEDIAL  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THREE MICROSCOPIC FOCI OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 31 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block D   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 AUG 03 at 14 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm round portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is oriented with two sutures  long suture designates lateral margin  short suture designates superior  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  Cut sections through the specimen show a firm white gray stellate mass which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm and is located 0 3cm from the nearest posterior margin  0 3cm from the medial margin  0 7cm from the inferior margin and more than 1 0cm from the anterior and the superior margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma consists of fibrous and adipose tissue and does not have any gross abnormality  The specimen is submitted as follows  A  The closest medial and posterior margin  B  The closest superior and anterior margin  C  The closest inferior and posterior margin  D  Representative section of the mass  E F  Representative sections of breast tissue away from the mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin lateral REMOVED_DATE of cavity   are three irregular pieces of fibroadipose tissue which measure in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimens are not oriented  One surface is irregular  granular and covered by shaggy fibrinous material and residual hemorrhage  The other surface of the specimen is smooth  The specimens are serially sectioned and submitted in entirety in cassettes G L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin medial REMOVED_DATE of cavity   consists of two irregular portions of fibroadipose tissue which measure in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimens are not oriented  serially sectioned  No gross abnormalities are noted  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes M T  Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT MEDIAL  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISIO PART C  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISI , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 27 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  95   SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AND EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID TYPE  5   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Much of the tumor grows as large solid nests  making the estimation of the proportions of in situ and invasive carcinoma somewhat imprecise  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm irregular piece of tan yellow tissue containing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm firm nodule which abuts a resection margin  Sectioning reveals the nodule as being well demarcated with a lobular surface  A portion of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  a piece of tissue is taken for electron microscopy  and the remainder of the tumor is submitted in A through D  with additional representative tissue in E through J  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA    NEUROENDOCRINE  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION    report_end  , Present.
