Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA  33 year old lady with left breast infiltrating ductal carcinoma with intraductal component  Re excision      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED INTRA OPERATIVE PATHOLOGIST Revised by  Teri L  Moore  MD Revised on 23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 07 15                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND FOREIGN BODY REACTION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is marked chronic inflammation with fat necrosis and histiocytic reaction in the permanent slide made from the frozen section tissue  however  carcinoma is not seen  It is not possible to locate the frozen section slide to confirm the frozen section diagnosis of malignancy  and it is possible the fat necrosis with inflammation represents the area interpreted as malignant on frozen section  AXILLA  LEFT  NODES   EXCISION  2 of 19 LYMPH NODES POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  MICROMETASTASES   Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lumpectomy specimen with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm with a central healed scar along its length  Two sutures designating the medial resection margin and one suture designating the superior resection margin are present  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm cavity that is lined by tan brown  shaggy surface  The cavity is 0 6cm from the medial resection margin  0 3cm from the inferior resection margin  0 6cm from the superior resection margin  1 9cm from the lateral resection margin and 1 6cm from the skin  A 0 5cm in greatest dimension  ill defined tan lesion is present just lateral to the cavity  Section Code  A  frozen section  1  B  medial resection margin  en face  C  cavity in relation to the superior resection margin  D  cavity in relation to the inferior resection margin  E  lateral resection margin en face  F    lesion  G M  90  of the cavity  N  the cavity in relation to the skin  O S  rest of the breast tissue  Also received fresh labeled  Left axilla nodes  is a 7 x 6 x 1cm piece of adipose tissue in which are found tan brown rubbery lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  entirely submitted in T through Y  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS      LEFT  BREAST  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2  FAT NECROSIS  3  THE INKED MARGIN IS FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   AXILLA NODE  LEFT    report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING MULTIFOCALLY TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is 1cm in greatest dimension  No unequivocal lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Estrogen receptor studies will be performed on formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tissue and will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   with attached specimen x ray   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing no gross lesion large enough to freeze  A 0 7cm ill  defined  slightly firm and gritty area is present at an inked margin  The nodule is submitted entirely in A through C  the remainder of the tissue in D through N  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Present.
